WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.416 --> 00:00:03.833 line:0%
Reporting live, I'm Kate Bradley,
Channel 12 News.

00:00:03.916 --> 00:00:05.458
You were meant for the bummer beat.

00:00:05.541 --> 00:00:08.333
<i>Fires, car crashes,
Black Friday riots at the mall.</i>

00:00:08.416 --> 00:00:09.416
Look out!

00:00:10.125 --> 00:00:12.875 position:58%
<i>The station management are going nuts
with all the risks you're taking.</i>

00:00:12.958 --> 00:00:15.500
-I call that being a reporter.
-It's got to stop.

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.875
There was a call from a woman
in the South Bronx

00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:21.583 position:56%
saying she found a bag full of cash.

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:24.416
She's convinced it was given to her
by a good Samaritan.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.083
Consider this a break
from the bummer beat.

00:00:28.041 --> 00:00:30.458
A woman finds a bag of money.
I mean, where's the story?

00:00:30.541 --> 00:00:32.499 position:61%
You don't buy the good Samaritan angle?

00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:35.125
I remain objective always. But, no.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.375
There is someone out there,
looking over and helping us.

00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:42.416
It's hard to believe that there's
somebody out there doing good deeds

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.291
and expecting nothing in return.

00:00:44.375 --> 00:00:47.416
It's real. I found it in front
of our front door this morning.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.666
He left the bag here.

00:00:49.458 --> 00:00:52.875 line:0%
<i>Just last week, eight people
found 100 grand on their doorsteps.</i>

00:00:52.958 --> 00:00:55.041 position:56%
We're looking for the good Samaritan
who's behind it.

00:00:55.916 --> 00:00:58.750
A woman started an anonymous
good Samaritan club.

00:00:58.833 --> 00:01:03.208 position:64%
And some guy in line at the grocery store
anonymously paid for the next ten people.

00:01:03.875 --> 00:01:05.499
<i>When I first got put on this story,</i>

00:01:05.583 --> 00:01:08.541
I was sure Good Sam
had some ulterior motive.

00:01:08.625 --> 00:01:11.250 position:61%
But there are way more people out there
doing good.

00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:24.166 position:59%
<i>Interest in Good Sam continues to grow
with these random acts of generosity</i>

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.541 position:63% line:0%
and when and where the next bag of money
might appear.

00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:31.625 position:66% line:0%
<i>People say New York City is a tough place.</i>

00:01:31.708 --> 00:01:35.666 position:59% line:0%
But thanks to Good Sam,
I see more kindness between strangers.

00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:40.875 position:56%
Good Sam is an inspiring hope.
In times like these, people need it.

00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:44.708
It's spreading, like miracles do.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.833
<i>The question at the top
of every New Yorker's mind,</i>

00:01:48.916 --> 00:01:50.666
"Good Sam, who are you?"

